#
# === #53 bilateral pair with docblock_coherent (recognition #53) ===
#
# Per `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]` (recognition
# #53): declarative property at
# `@epistemologic/property/<predicate>` + operational fracture body
# at `@kintsugi/fracture/<predicate>`, bridged by the kintsugi
# loop. THIS SHARD is the operational half of the sixth #53
# family's second-of-trio predicate: `docblock_coherent` (declarative
# half at TICK 5 `d158ca0`).
#
# Prior five #53 instances (per docblock_coherent shard's own
# ancestor tally):
#
# 1. `@kintsugi/fracture/keyword` (2026-06-10 `d908798`) — first.
# 2. `@mirror/fracture/predicate` (task #272 forward-promised).
# 3. `dark_count_monotone` (2026-06-19 `499ffd9`) — third.
# 4. `cold_compile_within_tolerance` (2026-06-19) — fourth.
# 5. `@kintsugi/surface` + `ashby_variety_match` (2026-07-03
#    `e910dd6`) — fifth.
#
# Sixth family's first operational half landed TICK 4 as
# `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded` (Seam RATIFY `9b0aeb5`);
# THIS is the sixth family's SECOND operational half, paired with
# `docblock_coherent` (declarative half at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/docblock_coherent.mirror`) landed
# TICK 5 `d158ca0`. The declarative side names WHAT it means for a
# docblock to be coherent; THIS operational side names WHAT TO DO
# when the docblock is incoherent — emits a Tomm-linear-then-reflexive
# question naming the two contradicting sites plus the frame at which
# they bind, via the `@kintsugi/surface` `contradiction` class.
#
# === Operational role: fracture body of docblock coherence ===
#
# When `docblock_coherent(d)` returns a failure verdict — either
# (arm 1) two extracted predicates from `d` mutually contradict at
# liquid-predicate altitude, OR (arm 2) an extracted predicate
# contradicts a below-seam declaration on the same shard `d.site`
# — this fracture body's action fires. The body's discharge shape:
#
#   incoherent docblock d
#     ⇒ kintsugi_lock_of(d, ctx) fires `contradiction`
#     ⇒ surface(d, contradiction, ctx) emits Tomm-linear-then-
#       reflexive question at reader-frame altitude naming both
#       contradicting sites (left ref, right ref) plus the frame
#       (bind ref) at which they meet at Bateson level `bateson_level`
#     ⇒ observation_depth returned as third-order witness
#
# The body is bilateral to `docblock_coherent`: the predicate's
# failure IS this body's activation site; this body's discharge
# closes the loop back to the predicate at the next kintsugi tick.
# No manual patching; no opaque carrier substitution; the closure
# rides `@kintsugi/surface`'s spawn branch via `contradiction`
# routing per `[[feedback-manual-closure-is-training-pull]]`.
#
# === contradiction surface class routing (compiler-error-surface §3.2) ===
#
# Per Mara's canonical spec `docs/math/kintsugi/compiler-error-
# surface.md` §3.2: `contradiction` is the surface class fired when
# two properties both fire success independently but their conjunction
# implies failure. Carnielli-Marcos LFI (2004, 2007) grounds the
# formal framing: `A ∧ ¬A ⊢ ⊥` in classical logic; in LFI, the
# substrate carries `○A` (consistency of A) as a separate operator,
# and `○A` at compile time IS `holds(gap)` per gap-tension-tensor-
# substrate §11 (`contradiction <= gap`).
#
# `contradiction` is THE ONE RIGOROUS surface class of the four (per
# compiler-error-surface §4.1 rigor table + candidate #142 reframing
# `2026-07-02`): its projection operator is DERIVED from the
# curvature 2-form `Ω = dω + ½[ω, ω]` — Ω splits as `dω_L + dω_R
# + [ω_L, ω_R]`; the `[ω_L, ω_R]` bracket IS the bind at Bateson
# level. Genuine derived projection onto the Bateson-level axis of
# the Lie-algebra-valued 2-form (curvature-and-tomm.md §5). The
# other three classes (ashby_mismatch / conundrum / out_of_band)
# await per-class projection-operator derivation as future arcs.
#
# Tomm shape (§5.3): linear-then-reflexive — the observer traces
# left's derivation and right's derivation independently (linear
# phase) and then names the frame at which they bind (reflexive
# phase). Bateson 1956 double-bind grounds the phase split:
# linear-in-each-message, reflexive-in-the-frame.
#
# A docblock claim that contradicts another docblock claim OR
# contradicts a below-seam declaration on the same shard IS a
# `contradiction` at doc-claim altitude: two liquid predicates both
# `holds` independently but the conjunction implies failure. The
# routing arm: `surface(d, contradiction, ctx)` per `@kintsugi/
# surface`'s three-mode-algebra spawn branch (spec §7.2 canonical
# signature); the discharge emits a Tomm-linear-then-reflexive
# question and returns an `observation_depth` witness. Per Mara
# spec §Cross-cutting Tomm question shapes: `docblock_incoherent_
# body`: Tomm linear-then-reflexive (§5.3) — name two sites,
# reflect on meeting boundary.
#
# The `requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)` clause on this
# fracture body IS the twelfth-instance discipline per
# `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`: the substrate had
# `ashby_variety_match(lock: lock_carrier) -> verdict` landed at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric.mirror`.
# We consume the landed ancestor; we do not invent a new predicate
# at doc-claim altitude. Same routing gate as
# `@kintsugi/surface.surface(...)`,
# `@kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm.resolve_restart_storm(...)`,
# and TICK 4's `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded.
# docblock_ungrounded_body(...)` per the fifth #53 witness's
# discipline (`e910dd6`).
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/docblock_incoherent.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_incoherent` at species-depth 2 under
# @kintsugi per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`. Same
# depth as the eleven landed sibling fracture bodies
# (`shards/kintsugi/fracture/{keyword,angle_to_paren,symbol_lift,
# operator_match,dark_count_monotone,cold_compile_within_tolerance,
# gate,partials_align,parent_cycle,restart_storm,docblock_ungrounded}
# .mirror`); this shard sits in the same species column and is
# subject to the same path-namespace pact. Sibling declarative half
# at `shards/epistemologic/property/docblock_coherent.mirror`
# (@epistemologic/property/docblock_coherent, species-depth 2 under
# @epistemologic) — bilateral coupling honours the family/species
# partition per `[[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-
# root]]`: form-side under @epistemologic; process-side under
# @kintsugi.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Per Mara's projection-surface spec `63bdecc` §6 the operator
# must audit its own audit at depth=3. THIS shard's own docblock
# is subject to `docblock_coherent(this_docblock)` at logical
# altitude — the exact predicate whose failure this shard's body
# routes. Substrate-honest verdict at THIS shard's state:
#
# Arm 1 (pairwise across `extract_predicates(this_docblock)`):
# the narrative above makes claims across multiple sections
# (bilateral #53 family membership; sixth-family/second-of-trio
# slot; operational role; contradiction routing; rigor asymmetry;
# path-namespace; twelfth-instance discipline). No two claims in
# the narrative contradict at analytical altitude — each section
# names distinct load-bearing content. Concrete `contradicts`-
# decidability awaits the extractor body (TICK 2 forward-promise)
# landing.
#
# Arm 2 (doc predicates vs `below_seam(this.site)` declarations):
# the narrative above claims `docblock_incoherent_body(d: docblock,
# ctx: kintsugi_context) -> ref requires ashby_variety_match
# (kintsugi_lock)`; the below-seam declaration IS
# `docblock_incoherent_body(d: docblock, ctx: kintsugi_context)
# -> ref requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock) { \ }`. The
# narrative names the `contradiction` routing class and the Tomm-
# linear-then-reflexive discharge shape; the below-seam glass
# declares the five-operation surface for the fracture_body action.
# No claim in the narrative contradicts a below-seam declaration
# on this shard. The `requires` clause's ancestor
# `ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)` lands at
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric` and is composed
# identically here.
#
