in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @kintsugi
in @kintsugi/surface
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property
in @epistemologic/property/docblock_coherent
in @docblock

glass @kintsugi/fracture/docblock_incoherent {
  focus fracture_body
  project fracture_body
  split fracture_body
  shift fracture_body
  settle fracture_body
}

# === docblock_incoherent_body (fracture body; operational half) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Reads a `docblock` d whose
# `docblock_coherent` verdict fired failure and a `kintsugi_context`
# ctx from the enclosing loop. Routes via `@kintsugi/surface`'s
# `contradiction` class per compiler-error-surface §3.2 — two
# liquid predicates (either two extracted from the docblock, or one
# extracted and one lifted from a below-seam declaration) both
# `holds` independently but their conjunction implies failure. The
# `contradiction` class is THE ONE RIGOROUS surface class of the
# four (§4.1 rigor table): its projection operator is DERIVED from
# `Ω = dω + ½[ω, ω]` — the `[ω,ω]` Bateson-bind IS the bracket
# term.
#
# Tomm shape (§5.3): linear-then-reflexive — trace L's derivation,
# trace R's derivation, then name the frame at which they bind
# (Bateson double-bind level-crossing). The surface emission fills
# the `contradiction` type carrier's four fields: `left: ref` (first
# claim), `right: ref` (second claim), `bind: ref` (level at which
# they meet), `bateson_level: nat` (Bateson logical type where bind
# fires).
#
# The `requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)` clause honours
# the twelfth-instance discipline per
# `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]`: same landed
# ancestor at `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric`
# consumed by `@kintsugi/surface.surface(...)`,
# `@kintsugi/fracture/restart_storm.resolve_restart_storm(...)`,
# and TICK 4's `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded.
# docblock_ungrounded_body(...)`.
#
# Body forward-promised per `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`;
# discharge composes over `surface(d, contradiction, ctx)` at the
# `\` obligation site when the extractor body (TICK 2 forward-
# promise `extract_predicate`) lands and a live doc_claim pair (or
# doc_claim + below-seam decl) fires the routing.
docblock_incoherent_body(d: docblock, ctx: kintsugi_context) -> ref
  requires ashby_variety_match(kintsugi_lock)
{ \ }

out @kintsugi/fracture/docblock_incoherent
out docblock_incoherent_body
